  A couple of things.  First, something I noticed in the PC version 
specifically.  The game starts out with everything at normal intensity.
However, the items are in high-intensity.  However, apparently the
hilighting is not turned off after drawing the item character, because
after that, all text is in high intensity.  This isn't really a problem,
and may actually be in the TERMCAP file provided, but if anyone has noticed
this on Unix, it may be a bug.

  Second, mimics are too easy to spot.  If you walk into a shop - you see
lots of armor, etc.  Then, if you walk out, any mimics will disappear,
but all the items remain.  Then, you can tell that the mimics are where
the empty spaces are.  This should probably be fixed, or else mimics are
too easy to avoid.

